    8: { sharp: "I'm not getting yelled at over dishes in front of half the house. If {a} wants a fight, {a} can have one at the vote.", dry: "Yelled at over dishes, in front of everyone. {a} can have a fight at the vote.",
      loud: "I'm NOT getting yelled at over DISHES in front of half the house! If {a} wants a fight, {a} gets one at the VOTE!", soft: "I'm not going to get yelled at over dishes in front of half the house. If {a} wants a fight, {a} can have one at the vote.",
      odd: "I got yelled at over dishes in front of half the house. Fine. The vote is where I do my dishes." },
